(2) Physical conditions:
1. Height: Applicants for large bus, heavy tractor-trailer, urban public bus, large truck, trolleybus permitted vehicle types shall have a height of 155 centimeters or above. Applicants for medium-sized bus permitted vehicle type shall have a height of 150 centimeters or above;
2. Vision: Applicants for large bus, heavy tractor-trailer, urban public bus, medium-sized bus, large truck, trolleybus or tram permitted vehicle types shall have uncorrected or corrected visual acuity of both eyes reaching 5.0 or above on the logarithmic visual acuity chart. Applicants for other permitted vehicle types shall have uncorrected or corrected visual acuity of both eyes reaching 4.9 or above on the logarithmic visual acuity chart. Those with monocular visual impairment whose better eye has uncorrected or corrected visual acuity reaching 5.0 or above on the logarithmic visual acuity chart and horizontal visual field reaching 150 degrees may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for small car, small automatic transmission car, low-speed truck, three-wheeled vehicle, disabled person's special small automatic transmission passenger car permitted vehicle types;
3. Color discrimination: No red-green color blindness;
4. Hearing: Each ear at a distance of 50 centimeters from a tuning fork can distinguish the direction of the sound source. Those with hearing impairment but wearing hearing aids can meet the above conditions may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for small car, small automatic transmission car permitted vehicle types;
5. Upper limbs: Both thumbs intact, each hand must have at least three other fingers intact, normal movement function of limbs and fingers. However, if the distal phalanx of a finger is missing or the left hand has three fingers intact and both palms are complete, one may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for small car, small automatic transmission car, low-speed truck, three-wheeled vehicle permitted vehicle types;
6. Lower limbs: Both lower limbs intact and normal movement function, unequal length not exceeding 5 centimeters. If only the left lower limb is missing or has lost movement function but the right lower limb is normal, one may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for small automatic transmission car permitted vehicle type;
7. Trunk, neck: No movement function impairment;
8. Right lower limb or both lower limbs missing or lost movement function but able to sit independently, and upper limbs comply with item 5 of this paragraph, one may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for disabled person's special small automatic transmission passenger car permitted vehicle type. If one palm is missing, the other hand's thumb is intact, other fingers have two fingers intact, upper limbs and fingers movement function normal, and lower limbs comply with item 6 of this paragraph, one may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for disabled person's special small automatic transmission passenger car permitted vehicle type;
9. Aged 70 years or above and able to pass tests of memory, judgment, reaction and other abilities, one may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license for small car, small automatic transmission car, disabled person's special small automatic transmission passenger car, light motorcycle permitted vehicle types.
Article 15: Under any of the following circumstances, one shall not apply for a motor vehicle driver's license:
(1) Having organic heart disease, epilepsy, Meniere's disease, vertigo, hysteria, paralysis agitans, mental illness, dementia, and nervous system diseases affecting limb movement and other diseases hindering safe driving;
(2) Having taken or injected drugs within three years or less than three years since the completion of compulsory drug rehabilitation measures, and long-term use of addictive psychotropic drugs without quitting;
(3) Escaping after causing a traffic accident constituting a crime;
(4) Driving a motor vehicle after drinking or while drunk causing a major traffic accident constituting a crime;
(5) Driving a motor vehicle while drunk or driving a commercial motor vehicle after drinking, and the motor vehicle driver's license has been revoked according to law for less than five years;
(6) Driving a commercial motor vehicle while drunk, and the motor vehicle driver's license has been revoked according to law for less than ten years;
(7) Driving a motor vehicle for chasing and racing, overloading, overspeeding, or transporting hazardous chemicals in violation of hazardous chemical safety management regulations constituting a crime, and the motor vehicle driver's license has been revoked according to law for less than five years;
(8) Causing a major traffic accident constituting a crime due to other violations of traffic management laws and regulations other than item 4 of this paragraph, and the motor vehicle driver's license has been revoked according to law for less than ten years;
(9) The motor vehicle driver's license has been revoked according to law for other circumstances for less than two years;
(10) Driving permission has been revoked according to law for less than three years;
(11) Driving a motor vehicle without a motor vehicle driver's license and causing a traffic accident with equal or greater responsibility resulting in serious injury or death of a person for less than ten years;
(12) Having acted as a substitute for another person in a motor vehicle driver's examination within three years;
(13) Other circumstances prescribed by laws and administrative regulations.
Driving a motor vehicle without a motor vehicle driver's license and having any of the behaviors in items 5 to 8 of the first paragraph, one shall not apply for a motor vehicle driver's license within the prescribed period.
Article 16: A person applying for a motor vehicle driver's license for the first time may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license with permitted vehicle types of urban public bus, large truck, small car, small automatic transmission car, low-speed truck, three-wheeled vehicle, disabled person's special small automatic transmission passenger car, ordinary three-wheeled motorcycle, ordinary two-wheeled motorcycle, light motorcycle, wheeled special-purpose machine, trolleybus, tram.
A person who already holds a motor vehicle driver's license and applies to add a permitted vehicle type may apply to add permitted vehicle types of large bus, heavy tractor-trailer, urban public bus, medium-sized bus, large truck, small car, small automatic transmission car, low-speed truck, three-wheeled vehicle, light tractor-trailer, ordinary three-wheeled motorcycle, ordinary two-wheeled motorcycle, light motorcycle, wheeled special-purpose machine, trolleybus, tram.
Article 17: A person who already holds a motor vehicle driver's license and applies to add a permitted vehicle type shall have no record of 12 points in the current scoring cycle and the most recent scoring cycle before application. Applying to add light tractor-trailer, medium-sized bus, heavy tractor-trailer, large bus permitted vehicle types shall also comply with the following provisions:
(1) Applying to add light tractor-trailer permitted

those of the permitted vehicle type, having obtained the qualification to drive small cars or small automatic transmission cars for more than one year;
(2) applying to add the permitted vehicle type of medium-sized buses, having obtained the qualification to drive urban buses, large trucks, small cars, small automatic transmission cars, low-speed cargo vehicles, or three-wheeled vehicles for more than two years, and having no record of reaching 12 points in the most recent two consecutive scoring cycles before the application;
(3) applying to add the permitted vehicle type of heavy tractor-trailers, having obtained the qualification to drive medium-sized buses or large trucks for more than two years, or having obtained the qualification to drive large buses for more than one year, and having no record of reaching 12 points in the most recent two consecutive scoring cycles before the application;
(4) applying to add the permitted vehicle type of large buses, having obtained the qualification to drive urban buses or medium-sized buses for more than two years, having obtained the qualification to drive large trucks for more than three years, or having obtained the qualification to drive heavy tractor-trailers for more than one year, and having no record of reaching 12 points in the most recent three consecutive scoring cycles before the application.

Students who are receiving full-time driving vocational education, have obtained the qualification to drive small cars at school, and have no record of reaching 12 points in the current scoring cycle and the most recent scoring cycle before the application, may apply to add the permitted vehicle types of large buses and heavy tractor-trailers.

Article 18: Under any of the following circumstances, one shall not apply for the permitted vehicle types of large buses, heavy tractor-trailers, urban buses, medium-sized buses, or large trucks:
(1) causing a traffic accident resulting in death and bearing equal or greater responsibility;
(2) driving a motor vehicle after drinking alcohol to the point of intoxication;
(3) driving a motor vehicle after drinking alcohol again;
(4) having the behavior of driving a motor vehicle after taking or injecting drugs, or having records of undergoing community drug rehabilitation, compulsory isolation drug rehabilitation, or community rehabilitation measures;
(5) driving a motor vehicle for chasing or racing, overloading, speeding, or transporting hazardous chemicals in violation of hazardous chemical safety management regulations constituting a crime;
(6) having had a motor vehicle driver's license revoked or cancelled for less than ten years;
(7) driving a motor vehicle without a motor vehicle driver's license and causing a traffic accident bearing equal or greater responsibility resulting in serious injury or death to persons.

Article 19: Holders of motor vehicle driver's licenses issued by the military or the Chinese People's Armed Police Force who meet the application conditions of these provisions may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license of the corresponding permitted vehicle type.

Article 20: Holders of foreign motor vehicle driver's licenses who meet the application conditions of these provisions, and who have cumulatively resided for ninety days or more within one year in the issuing country or region at the time of obtaining such driver's license, may apply for a motor vehicle driver's license of the corresponding permitted vehicle type. Those applying for a motor vehicle driver's license of the permitted vehicle types of large buses, heavy tractor-trailers, or medium-sized buses shall also have obtained a foreign motor vehicle driver's license of the corresponding permitted vehicle type for more than two years.

Article 21: Holders of foreign motor vehicle driver's licenses who need to temporarily drive motor vehicles shall apply to the vehicle management office for a temporary motor vehicle driving permit in accordance with regulations.

For those entering the country for a short stay, a temporary motor vehicle driving permit with a validity period of three months may be applied for; for those whose stay or residence period exceeds three months, the validity period may be extended to one year.

If a temporarily entering motor vehicle driver accumulates 12 points within one scoring cycle on their temporary motor vehicle driving permit and does not participate in the study and examination of road traffic safety laws, regulations, and related knowledge as prescribed, they shall not apply for a motor vehicle driver's license or apply again for a temporary motor vehicle driving permit.

Article 22: Persons applying for a motor vehicle driver's license shall submit an application to the vehicle management office in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) those residing at their place of household registration shall apply at their place of household registration;
(2) those residing outside their place of household registration may apply at their place of residence;
(3) active-duty military personnel (including the Chinese People's Armed Police Force) shall apply at the location of their military unit;
(4) foreign nationals shall apply at their place of residence or domicile;
(5) those applying to add a permitted vehicle type shall apply at the place where their motor vehicle driver's license was issued;
(6) those receiving full-time driving vocational education and applying to add the permitted vehicle types of large buses or heavy tractor-trailers shall apply at the place where they are receiving education.

Article 23: When applying for a motor vehicle driver's license, the applicant shall confirm the application information and submit the following certificates:
(1) the applicant's identity certificate;
(2) a certificate regarding physical condition issued by a medical institution.

Article 24: Persons holding motor vehicle driver's licenses issued by the military or the Chinese People's Armed Police Force who apply for a motor vehicle driver's license shall confirm the application information and submit the following certificates and vouchers:
(1) the applicant's identity certificate. Those who are demobilized, transferred, or discharged from military service shall also submit the demobilization, transfer, or discharge certificate issued by the military or the Chinese People's Armed Police Force;
(2) a certificate regarding physical condition issued by a medical institution;
(3) the motor vehicle driver's license issued by the military or the Chinese People's Armed Police Force.

Article 25: Persons holding foreign motor vehicle driver's licenses who apply for a motor vehicle driver's license shall confirm the application information and submit the following certificates and vouchers:
(1) the applicant's identity certificate;
(2) a certificate regarding physical condition issued by a medical institution;
(3) the motor vehicle driver's license held. If it is not expressed in Chinese, a Chinese translation text issued by a translation agency or notarized by a notary public shall also be provided.

Applications by personnel of foreign embassies and consulates in China and personnel of representative offices of international organizations in China shall be handled in accordance with the principle of diplomatic reciprocity.

Applications by residents of the mainland shall also submit the applicant's passport or exit-entry permit for traveling to and from Hong Kong and Macao, or exit-entry permit for traveling to and from Taiwan.

