The self-study and direct examination management system for driver's licenses for small automobiles and small automatic transmission automobiles shall be separately prescribed by the Ministry of Public Security.
Article 27 A person applying for a motor vehicle driver's license who meets the driving license conditions required by these provisions and falls under any of the following circumstances may directly apply for the examination for a motor vehicle driver's license for the corresponding authorized vehicle type in accordance with the provisions of paragraph 1 of Article 16 and Article 23:
(1) the original motor vehicle driver's license was cancelled due to failure to renew it upon expiration of its validity period;
(2) the original motor vehicle driver's license was cancelled due to failure to submit a physical condition certificate;
(3) the original motor vehicle driver's license was cancelled upon the holder's own application;
(4) the original motor vehicle driver's license was cancelled due to temporary non-compliance with physical condition requirements;
(5) the original motor vehicle driver's license or authorized vehicle type qualification was cancelled for other reasons, except where the motor vehicle driver's license was revoked or rescinded;
(6) the holder of a motor vehicle driver's license issued by the military or the Chinese People's Armed Police Force whose validity period has expired;
(7) the holder of a foreign motor vehicle driver's license or a foreign motor vehicle driver's license whose validity period has expired.
A person falling under any of the circumstances specified in items (6) and (7) of the preceding paragraph shall also submit a motor vehicle driver's license.
Article 28 Where the proofs and vouchers submitted by the applicant are complete and conform to the statutory form, the vehicle administration office shall accept them and examine the applicant's conditions for applying for a motor vehicle driver's license in accordance with the provisions. Where the circumstances specified in Article 25 apply, the exit and entry records of the applicant shall also be verified; where any of the circumstances specified in items (1) to (5) of paragraph 1 of Article 27 applies, the driving experience of the applicant shall also be verified; where the applicant is a student receiving full-time driving vocational education and applies to add the authorized vehicle types of large buses or heavy tractor-trailers, the student status of the applicant shall also be verified.
Where the public security organ traffic management department has already realized online verification with medical institutions and other units, the applicant is exempt from submitting proofs and vouchers such as physical condition certificates.
For those who meet the application conditions, the vehicle administration office shall arrange the examination appointment in accordance with the provisions; where no examination is required, the motor vehicle driver's license shall be issued within one day. Where an applicant who is a demobilized, transferred, or retired military personnel applies for a motor vehicle driver's license using a motor vehicle driver's license issued by the military or the Chinese People's Armed Police Force, the military or Chinese People's Armed Police Force motor vehicle driver's license shall be recovered.
Article 29 Where the vehicle administration office has doubts about the application conditions of the applicant, the submitted materials, or the declared matters, it may investigate and verify the substantive content.
During the investigation, the applicant shall be interviewed and an interview record shall be made, and the issuing authority of the proofs and vouchers shall be verified.
Upon investigation, if the applicant does not meet the application conditions, the application shall not be processed; if there is an illegal act, it shall be handled in accordance with the law.
Chapter 3 Examination of Motor Vehicle Drivers
Section 1 Examination Content and Passing Standards
Article 30 The examination content for motor vehicle drivers is divided into the examination subject on road traffic safety laws, regulations, and related knowledge (hereinafter referred to as "Subject 1"), the examination subject on field driving skills (hereinafter referred to as "Subject 2"), and the examination subject on road driving skills and safe and civilized driving knowledge (hereinafter referred to as "Subject 3").
A person who already holds a driver's license for the authorized vehicle type of small automatic transmission automobiles and applies to add the authorized vehicle type of small automobiles shall be examined on Subject 2 and Subject 3.
A person who already holds a driver's license for the authorized vehicle types of large buses, urban public buses, medium-sized buses, large trucks, small automobiles, or small automatic transmission automobiles and applies to add the authorized vehicle type of light tractor-trailers shall be examined on Subject 2 and the safe and civilized driving knowledge of Subject 3.
A person who already holds a driver's license for the authorized vehicle type of light motorcycles and applies to add the authorized vehicle types of ordinary three-wheeled motorcycles or ordinary two-wheeled motorcycles, or a person who holds a driver's license for ordinary two-wheeled motorcycles and applies to add the authorized vehicle type of ordinary three-wheeled motorcycles, shall be examined on Subject 2 and Subject 3.
Where the physical condition of a motor vehicle driver who already holds a driver's license for the authorized vehicle types of large buses, heavy tractor-trailers, urban public buses, medium-sized buses, large trucks, small automobiles, or small automatic transmission automobiles changes, such that they no longer meet the conditions for the authorized vehicle type of the motor vehicle driver's license they hold, but meet the conditions for the authorized vehicle type of small automatic transmission passenger cars specially designed for persons with disabilities, and they apply for a change, they shall be examined on Subject 2 and Subject 3.
Article 31 The examination content and passing standards are unified nationwide, and corresponding examination items are prescribed according to different authorized vehicle types.
Article 32 The examination content of Subject 1 includes: road passage, traffic signals, road traffic safety illegal acts and traffic accident handling, application for and use of motor vehicle driver's licenses, motor vehicle registration and other provisions, as well as other road traffic safety laws, regulations, and rules.
Article 33 The examination content of Subject 2 includes:
(1) for large buses, heavy tractor-trailers, urban public buses, medium-sized buses, and large trucks: pile test, hill start and stop, side parking, passing through a single-side bridge, curve driving, right-angle turn, passing through a width-limiting gate, U-turn on a narrow road, as well as simulated expressway, continuous sharp curves in mountainous areas, tunnels, rainy (foggy) weather, slippery roads, and emergency disposal;
(2) for small automobiles and low-speed cargo vehicles: reversing into a garage, hill start and stop, side parking, curve driving, right-angle turn;
(3) for small automatic transmission automobiles and small automatic transmission passenger cars specially designed for persons with disabilities: reversing into a garage, side parking, curve driving, right-angle turn;
(4) for light tractor-trailers: pile test, curve driving, right-angle turn;
(5) for three-wheeled automobiles, ordinary three-wheeled motorcycles, ordinary two-wheeled motorcycles, and light motorcycles: pile test, hill start and stop, passing through a single-side bridge;
(6) for wheeled special-purpose machinery vehicles, trolleybuses, trams

Drivers of motor vehicles who require corrective lenses shall wear glasses when driving motor vehicles.

Article 79 Where a motor vehicle driver falls under any of the following circumstances, the vehicle administration office shall cancel his or her motor vehicle driver's license:

(1) Death;

(2) Submission of an application for cancellation;

(3) Loss of civil capacity for conduct, and the guardian submits an application for cancellation;

(4) Physical condition is not suitable for driving a motor vehicle;

(5) Suffering from organic heart disease, epilepsy, Meniere's disease, vertigo, hysteria, paralysis agitans, mental illness, dementia, and other diseases of the nervous system affecting limb movement that hinder safe driving;

(6) Being found to have driven a motor vehicle after taking or injecting drugs, and being ordered by law to undergo community drug rehabilitation or community recovery, or being decided to undergo compulsory isolation for drug rehabilitation, or being addicted to long-term use of psychotropic drugs causing dependence and not yet having quit;

(7) Substituting for another person to take the motor vehicle driver's examination;

(8) More than one year has passed since the expiration of the motor vehicle driver's license without renewal;

(9) Being over 70 years of age and failing to submit a physical condition certificate within one year after the end of a scoring cycle; or holding a driving license for a small automatic passenger car specially designed for persons with disabilities and failing to submit a physical condition certificate within one year after the end of three scoring cycles;

(10) Being over 63 years of age, and the motor vehicle driver's license held only contains the authorized vehicle type of wheeled special-purpose machinery vehicle, trolleybus, or tram, and no application for extension has been approved by the vehicle administration office; or being over 70 years of age, and the motor vehicle driver's license held only contains the authorized vehicle type of low-speed truck or three-wheeled automobile;

(11) The motor vehicle driver's license has been lawfully revoked or the driving permission has been lawfully cancelled.

Where any of the circumstances in items 2 to 11 of the first paragraph exists and the motor vehicle driver's license has not been recovered, the motor vehicle driver's license shall be announced as invalid.

Where a motor vehicle driver's license is cancelled due to the circumstance in item 8 of the first paragraph and the cancellation has not exceeded two years, the motor vehicle driver may resume driving qualification after passing the examination on road traffic safety laws, regulations, and related knowledge. The applicant may apply to the vehicle administration office at the place of issuance of the motor vehicle driver's license or at a place other than the place of issuance.

Where a motor vehicle driver's license is cancelled due to the circumstance in item 9 of the first paragraph, and the motor vehicle driver's license is within its validity period or has expired for less than one year, the motor vehicle driver may resume driving qualification after submitting a physical condition certificate. The applicant may apply to the vehicle administration office at the place of issuance of the motor vehicle driver's license or at a place other than the place of issuance.

Where any of the circumstances in items 2 to 9 of the first paragraph exists, and an application for a motor vehicle driver's license is made in accordance with Article 27, if there are records of road traffic safety violations or traffic accidents that have not been handled, the road traffic safety violations and traffic accidents shall be handled first.

Article 80 Where a road traffic safety violation committed by a motor vehicle driver during the probationary period is recorded as 12 points, the driving qualification for the probationary authorized vehicle type shall be cancelled.

Article 81 Where information such as the contact telephone number and contact address of a motor vehicle driver changes, the driver shall file the change with the vehicle administration office at the place of issuance of the driver's license within 30 days after the change.

Where information such as the employing unit of a driver holding a driver's license for a large passenger bus, heavy tractor-trailer, urban public bus, medium passenger bus, or large truck changes, the change shall be filed with the vehicle administration office at the place of the employing unit within 30 days after the change.

Article 82 Road transport enterprises shall regularly file the employed motor vehicle drivers with the public security organ traffic management department at their location, and urge them to handle road traffic safety violations, traffic accidents, and participate in motor vehicle driver's license review and verification in a timely manner.

The public security organ traffic management department shall notify the transportation competent department and transport enterprises within its jurisdiction every month of the road traffic safety violations, points, and traffic accidents of motor vehicle drivers.

Article 83 Where a vehicle administration office discovers any of the following circumstances in the process of handling driver's license issuance and related business, it shall promptly carry out an investigation:

(1) Suspected submission of false application materials;

(2) Suspected bribery or cheating during the examination process;

(3) Suspected obtaining a motor vehicle driver's license by deception, bribery, or other improper means;

(4) Suspected use of forged or altered motor vehicle driver's licenses;

(5) Abnormal circumstances such as frequent replacement or reissuance, transfer-out or transfer-in of driver's licenses within a short period;

(6) Other illegal or non-compliant circumstances.

Where a vehicle administration office discovers that an applicant handling driver's license replacement or reissuance through the Internet has suspected circumstances as prescribed in the preceding paragraph, it shall convert it to on-site handling, examine the application materials on the spot, and promptly carry out an investigation.

Article 84 When carrying out an investigation, a vehicle administration office may notify the applicant to assist in the investigation, inquire about the suspected circumstances, record the investigation content, and may take measures such as on-site inspection, retrieval of files, and retrieval of examination video monitoring for verification.

Where it is discovered through investigation that an administrative case or criminal case is involved, necessary coercive measures or other disposal measures shall be taken in accordance with the law, and the case shall be transferred to the public security organ with jurisdiction for handling in accordance with the "Provisions of Public Security Organs on Handling Administrative Cases," "Provisions of Public Security Organs on Handling Criminal Cases," and other relevant regulations.

Article 85 When handling business for driver's licenses for small automatic passenger cars specially designed for persons with disabilities, the submitted physical condition certificate shall be issued by a specialized medical institution recognized by the provincial health administrative department. When handling business for other motor vehicle driver's licenses, the submitted physical condition certificate shall be issued by a medical institution at the county level or above the regiment level of the armed forces, or by a medical institution with health examination qualifications at the secondary level or above, such as a hospital, township health center, community health service center, or health examination center recognized by the health administrative department at the municipal level or above.

The physical condition certificate is valid within six months from the date of issuance.

The public security organ traffic management department shall, in conjunction with the health

health administrative department shall publish in office premises and on the Internet the names, addresses, and contact information of medical institutions within its jurisdiction that may issue physical condition certificates.
Article 86 Where a medical institution issues a false physical condition certificate, the public security organ traffic management department shall cease to recognize certificates issued by such medical institution and shall notify the health administrative department.
Section 3 Management of School Bus Drivers
Article 87 School bus drivers shall obtain school bus driving qualifications in accordance with the law.
To obtain school bus driving qualifications, the following conditions shall be met:
(1) holding a driver's license for the corresponding authorized vehicle type and having more than three years of driving experience, with age meeting the national conditions for school bus driving qualifications;
(2) no record of having been assessed 12 points during each of the last three consecutive scoring cycles;
(3) no record of responsibility for a traffic accident causing death or serious injury;
(4) no record of driving a motor vehicle while drunk or intoxicated, and no record of serious road traffic safety violations such as overloading or speeding while driving a passenger transport vehicle within the last year;
(5) no criminal record;
(6) sound physical and mental health, no infectious diseases, no history of diseases such as epilepsy or mental illness that may endanger driving safety, and no record of alcohol abuse or drug use.
Article 88 A motor vehicle driver applying for school bus driving qualifications shall submit an application to the public security organ traffic management department at the county level or at the city level divided into districts, confirm the application information, and submit the following certificates and vouchers:
(1) the applicant's identity certificate;
(2) the motor vehicle driver's license;
(3) a certificate concerning physical condition issued by a medical institution.
Article 89 The public security organ traffic management department shall, within five days from the date of accepting the application, examine the submitted certificates and vouchers, and verify with the public security organ at the county level where the applicant is located to confirm that the applicant has no criminal record or record of drug use. For those meeting the conditions, an endorsement permitting the driving of school buses and the corresponding vehicle type shall be made on the motor vehicle driver's license, and the education administrative department shall be notified; for those not meeting the conditions, the reasons shall be stated in writing.
Article 90 School bus drivers shall, within 30 days after the end of each scoring cycle, undergo review and verification at the public security organ traffic management department. During the review and verification, they shall submit a certificate concerning physical condition issued by a medical institution, participate in not less than three hours of study on road traffic safety laws and regulations, civilized traffic safety driving, emergency disposal, and other knowledge, and accept traffic accident case warning education.
Article 91 The public security organ traffic management department shall establish an information exchange mechanism with the education administrative department and schools, and shall notify the education administrative department and schools monthly of school bus drivers' traffic violations, traffic accidents, and review and verification situations.
Article 92 Where a school bus driver falls under any of the following circumstances, the public security organ traffic management department shall cancel their school bus driving qualification, notify the motor vehicle driver to exchange for a motor vehicle driver's license, and notify the education administrative department and the school:
(1) applying for cancellation;
(2) exceeding the age limit for national school bus driving qualification conditions;
(3) bearing responsibility for a traffic accident causing death or serious injury;
(4) driving a motor vehicle while drunk or intoxicated, and committing serious road traffic safety violations such as overloading or speeding while driving a passenger transport vehicle;
(5) having a record of being assessed 12 points or a criminal record;
(6) having an infectious disease, epilepsy, mental illness, or other diseases that may endanger driving safety, or having a record of alcohol abuse or drug use.
Where the motor vehicle driver's license endorsed with permission to drive a school bus is not recovered, the school bus driving qualification shall be announced as invalid.
Chapter 6 Legal Liability
Article 93 Where an applicant conceals relevant circumstances or provides false materials to apply for a motor vehicle driver's license, the public security organ traffic management department shall not accept or shall not handle the application, and shall impose a fine of not more than 500 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for a motor vehicle driver's license again within one year.
Where an applicant engages in bribery or cheating during the examination process, the examination qualification shall be cancelled, the results of other subjects already passed shall be invalid, and the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for a motor vehicle driver's license again within one year.
Where an applicant obtains a motor vehicle driver's license by deception, bribery, or other improper means, the public security organ traffic management department shall confiscate the motor vehicle driver's license, revoke the motor vehicle driving permission, and impose a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for a motor vehicle driver's license again within three years.
Where any of the acts in the preceding three paragraphs is organized or participated in for the purpose of obtaining economic benefits, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not less than three times but not more than five times the illegal income, but the maximum shall not exceed 100,000 yuan.
Where an applicant conceals relevant circumstances or provides false materials to apply for school bus driving qualifications, the public security organ traffic management department shall not accept or shall not handle the application, and shall impose a fine of not more than 500 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for school bus driving qualifications again within one year. Where an applicant obtains school bus driving qualifications by deception, bribery, or other improper means, the public security organ traffic management department shall revoke the school bus driving qualifications and impose a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan; the applicant shall not apply for school bus driving qualifications again within three years.
Article 94 Where an applicant, under the guidance of an instructor or a designated guidance personnel marked with a learner sign in the vehicle, uses a motor vehicle conforming to regulations to learn driving and commits a road traffic safety violation or causes a traffic accident, liability shall be borne by the instructor or the guidance personnel in the vehicle in accordance with Article 20 of the Regulations for the Implementation of the Road Traffic Safety Law.
Article 95 Where an applicant, while learning to drive on a road, falls under any of the following circumstances, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not less than 20 yuan but not more than 200 yuan on the instructor or the guidance personnel in the vehicle:
(1) not conducted according to the route and time designated by the public security organ traffic management department;
(2) failing to place or affix the learner sign in accordance with Article 42 of these Provisions.
Article 96

When learning to drive on a road, if any of the following circumstances exist, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not less than 200 yuan but not more than 500 yuan on the instructor or the person providing guidance in the vehicle:
(1) A motor vehicle not complying with the prescribed requirements is used;
(2) A vehicle used for self-study carries persons other than the person providing guidance in the vehicle.

Article 97: When an applicant learns to drive on a road, if any of the following circumstances exists, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose penalties in accordance with the provisions of Article 99, Paragraph 1, Item 1 of the "Road Traffic Safety Law":
(1) The applicant has not obtained a learner's permit;
(2) There is no instructor or person providing guidance in the vehicle;
(3) The person providing guidance in the vehicle does not meet the prescribed requirements.

If a motor vehicle is entrusted to an applicant who has any of the circumstances specified in the preceding paragraph for driving, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose penalties in accordance with the provisions of Article 99, Paragraph 1, Item 2 of the "Road Traffic Safety Law".

Article 98: If a motor vehicle driver commits any of the following acts, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not less than 20 yuan but not more than 200 yuan:
(1) After supplementing or replacing a motor vehicle driver's license, the driver continues to use the original motor vehicle driver's license;
(2) During the probationary period, driving a motor vehicle in non-compliance with the provisions of Article 77;
(3) A driver holding a driver's license for large buses, heavy tractors, urban public buses, medium-sized buses, or large trucks fails to report changes in information in accordance with the provisions of Article 81.

If the circumstance specified in Paragraph 1, Item 1 of this Article exists, the public security organ traffic management department shall recover the original motor vehicle driver's license.

Article 99: If a motor vehicle driver commits any of the following acts, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not less than 200 yuan but not more than 500 yuan:
(1) During the period in which the motor vehicle driver's license has been lawfully detained, withheld, or temporarily suspended, the driver applies for a replacement license by means of concealment or deception;
(2) The physical condition of the motor vehicle driver changes such that they are no longer suitable for driving a motor vehicle, yet they continue to drive a motor vehicle;
(3) The driver fails to participate in the review within the prescribed time limit and continues to drive a motor vehicle.

If any of the circumstances specified in Paragraph 1, Item 1 or Item 2 of this Article exists, the public security organ traffic management department shall recover the motor vehicle driver's license.

Article 100: If a motor vehicle driver engages in fraud when signing learning records or during the learning process while participating in review education, the corresponding learning record shall be invalid, the driver shall participate in review learning again, and the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not more than 1,000 yuan.

If a person substitutes for the actual motor vehicle driver to participate in review education, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not more than 2,000 yuan.

If a person organizes others to commit any of the acts specified in the preceding two paragraphs and has illegal income, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not more than three times the illegal income, but the maximum shall not exceed 20,000 yuan; if there is no illegal income, the public security organ traffic management department shall impose a fine of not more than 20,000 yuan.

Article 101: The public security departments of provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government may, based on the actual conditions of their respective regions and within the scope of the penalty limits prescribed in these provisions, formulate specific implementation standards.

The handling procedures for road traffic safety violations prescribed in these provisions shall be carried out in accordance with the "Provisions on the Procedures for Handling Road Traffic Safety Violations".

Article 102: Public security organ traffic management departments and their traffic police and auxiliary police officers shall accept supervision lawfully implemented by supervisory organs, public security organ inspection and audit departments, etc., when handling motor vehicle driver's license business and conducting motor vehicle driver examinations.

Public security organ traffic management departments and their traffic police and auxiliary police officers shall consciously accept supervision from society and citizens when handling motor vehicle driver's license business and conducting motor vehicle driver examinations.

Article 103: If traffic police have any of the following circumstances, they shall be given sanctions in accordance with relevant regulations; if hired personnel have any of the following circumstances, they shall be dismissed. If a crime is constituted, criminal responsibility shall be investigated in accordance with the law:
(1) Signing off on qualified examination results or issuing motor vehicle driver's licenses for persons who do not meet the conditions for motor vehicle driving permission, who have not taken the examination, or who have failed the examination;
(2) Reducing examination items, lowering evaluation standards, or participating in, assisting, or conniving at examination cheating;
(3) Issuing learner's permits or learner-specific signs to applicants who do not meet the prescribed requirements;
(4) Colluding with illegal intermediaries to seek economic benefits;
(5) Violating regulations by intruding into the motor vehicle driver's license management system, leaking, altering, or trading system data, or leaking system passwords;
(6) Violating regulations by selling or providing motor vehicle driver's license information to others;
(7) Participating in or indirectly participating in the business operations of driving training institutions, social examination sites, or examination equipment production and sales enterprises;
(8) Taking advantage of their position to demand or accept property from others or to seek other benefits.

If traffic police fail to use law enforcement recorders in accordance with the provisions of Article 53, Paragraph 1, they shall be given sanctions in accordance with relevant regulations based on the severity of the circumstances.

If a public security organ traffic management department has any of the acts listed in Paragraph 1, corresponding sanctions shall be given to the directly responsible supervisors and other directly responsible personnel in accordance with relevant regulations.

Chapter 7 Supplementary Provisions

Article 104: If there are mutual recognition agreements between states regarding motor vehicle driver's licenses, they shall be handled in accordance with the agreement.

If relevant agreements involving motor vehicle driver's licenses are signed between states, they shall be implemented in accordance with the agreement.

Article 105: Motor vehicle drivers may entrust agents to handle license replacement, replacement of lost licenses, submission of physical condition certificates, submission of review materials, extension of handling, and cancellation business. When an agent applies for motor vehicle driver's license business, they shall submit the agent's identity certificate and the motor vehicle driver's power of attorney.

Article 106: Public security organ traffic management departments shall implement electronic management of driver examination and driver's license management files. Electronic files of motor vehicle driver's licenses shall have the same legal effect as paper files.

